## What to Record Before Asking for Help

Write down the exact message you see, when the problem started, your Windows version, the device model if an accessory is involved, and every fix you already tried. This makes it easier for a support person to separate a Windows setting problem from a hardware, driver, account, network, or app problem.

If the problem comes and goes, also record the pattern. Note whether it happens after sleep mode, restart, an update, connecting a device, moving to another Wi-Fi network, or opening one specific app. Clear notes prevent repeated risky steps and help you stop before changing advanced settings.

## Advanced Fixes

Back up important files before advanced fixes. Stop if you see missing files, BitLocker recovery, repeated blue screens, or drive errors.

